coverage:
I read all eight sections in full and re-derived each step of the induction for n>=5.
- Cone reduction: product-lemma algebra; smooth puncture via lower semicontinuity and the induction (p_N<p_n); index 1 from d<=1/q with p_n>1/2; Gorenstein generator.
- Small-stabilizer case:
  - integrality of em/l, giving e=1 and l=m;
  - the orbifold Riemann–Roch value chi, checked on O(1) and O(m) over P(1,m) (the sign convention for characters does not matter);
  - finite evaluation and the symmetric tensor of weight -bm;
  - Bochner/subharmonicity bound tau>=-b (sharp on C^n), uniform character estimate, rounding to nm=r, then Kobayashi–Ochiai.
- Jet section:
  - test valuation discrepancy N+N*delta, checked through the chart canonical form;
  - F(0)=N^n s H, checked on C^n (gives n^n);
  - moment identities and the near-minimality derivative argument;
  - envelope formula and the stationarity, size-bias and Hessian computations in the critical-point lemma;
  - escape to infinity via Grünbaum, scalar formula Phi_inf and its maximum at t=2. I checked the scalar formula numerically, and random and exceptional-vector Monte Carlo searches all stayed below C*=1.93916<2. Rational certificate checked.
- Adjoint lifting:
  - positivity identity (j+r-j0)pi^*L and weighted-blowup canonical class;
  - Howald chart computation and the pushdown/initial recovery;
  - saturation via recurrence and height-one facets. Sanity check on the quadric: Gamma={j>=sum_{i<N}x_i+x_N/2}, Hilbert count matches, facet 2j-2sum x-x_N has height 1, Gamma is Gorenstein.
- Filtrations: Rees canonical form lambda^{-Q} (checked on C[x]); reducedness bound (N+1/2)^{N+1}<2N^{N+1}; G=D[v] multiplicativity; canonical shift n; free-grading lemma.
- Bootstrap: A_C(w)<=N*l+A_Y(u), including the lower bound A_{C×A^1}(V)>=A_C(w)+l via retractions; vol(w)<=l^{-n}; equal per-character shares; injection into a single character piece; the closed-form minimum over x and the Hölder step, giving d<=p_n/2+M_n/2. Checked against the paper's ODP example, where equality holds exactly. Slice klt and singularity arguments, equality case, strict-count and rounding lemmas, and the hypersurface endgame.
